FAQ = [
 ("What is the best LED light kit for a 2021–2026 Bronco?",
  "For most owners, the Baja Designs Squadron Pro A-pillar kit. Baja lists two Squadron Pro lights at 4,095 lumens and 41.4 watts each, a relay harness with a toggle switch, stainless hardware and wide cornering lenses in the box, and says the mount needs no cutting or drilling. It fits the 2021–2026 Bronco and the 2022–2026 Bronco Raptor, starting at $519.95. A-pillar lights sit low and to the sides, so they light trail edges well and bounce less glare off the hood than a roof bar."),
 ("Will a Bronco Sport light bar kit fit the full-size Bronco?",
  "No. The Bronco Sport is a separate compact crossover with a different body, windshield and roof. Rigid and Baja both sell Bronco Sport kits with titles that look almost identical to the full-size Bronco versions, such as Rigid's Bronco Sport CX430 roof kit and Baja's Bronco Sport A-pillar kit. Read the listing title for \"Bronco Sport\" or \"CX430\" before you order, and buy only parts that name the full-size 2021+ Bronco."),
 ("Does my Bronco have factory upfitter switches?",
  "Many do. Ford Authority reports six pre-wired switches in the overhead console: one 30 amp, one 15 amp and four 10 amp fused circuits, about 100 amps in total. They were standard on the Black Diamond, Wildtrak and Badlands at launch and optional on the Base and Outer Banks. Wires terminate at points under the hood, in the glovebox, at the A-pillar and in the rear cargo area. Look at your overhead console: if there are six AUX buttons, buy the upfitter harness version of your kit."),
 ("Can I wire a light bar straight to a Bronco upfitter switch?",
  "Only if the circuit is rated for the light. Rigid's 40 in SR kit is rated at 18.5 amps at 14 volts, which is more than the 15 amp and 10 amp circuits Ford Authority lists, so it would need the 30 amp circuit or its own relay triggered by a smaller switch. A pair of Baja Squadron Pro pods draws about 6 amps, which suits a 10 or 15 amp switch. When in doubt, let the upfitter switch trigger a relay and run the light's power from the battery through its own fuse."),
 ("Are LED light bars legal to use on the road in a Bronco?",
  "Usually not while driving. Many states treat light bars and most auxiliary pods as off-road lights: they must be switched off on public roads, and some states also require an opaque cover. States also commonly limit how many auxiliary lamps you can run and how high they can be mounted, and KC HiLiTES notes that mounting at or below headlight height avoids most problems. SAE-marked fog lights such as Baja's Squadron SAE are designed for road use. Check your own state's rules before switching anything on in traffic."),
 ("Will a steel-bumper fog pocket kit fit my Bronco's plastic bumper?",
  "No. Baja says its Squadron SAE and dual S2 Sport fog pocket kit is for the OE steel bumper only and is not compatible with plastic or modular bumpers. Broncos left the factory with different front bumpers depending on trim and options; Wikipedia notes the Badlands came with a powder-coated steel front bumper and LED fogs. Look at your bumper, or check your window sticker, before you buy a pocket kit."),
 ("Do I need to drill to mount a light bar on a Bronco?",
  "Not with the kits on this page. Baja says its A-pillar kits need no cutting or drilling, Quadratec describes Rigid's roof-rack kit as drill-free using existing mounting points, and the fog pocket kit replaces the factory fog facia mounts. Budget windshield brackets usually bolt to the windshield frame and A-pillar hardware, but read the listing and install sheet first, because some universal brackets need a hole for the harness grommet."),
 ("How much light do I actually need on a Bronco?",
  "It depends on speed and terrain. Rigid's 40 in SR bar is rated at 25,080 raw lumens, which suits open desert and fast fire roads. Baja's Squadron Pro pods are 4,095 lumens each, and the XL80 pods 9,022 lumens each. On slow, twisty trails, a pair of wide-beam A-pillar pods lights the corners where you steer. For fast open terrain, a roof-line bar or long-range spot pods reach farther. Many owners pair low pods for width with one long-range light for reach."),
 ("Will a roof light bar make wind noise on my Bronco?",
  "It can. None of the maker pages publish noise figures, but a bar in the airflow above the windshield is the most likely setup to whistle or hum. Quadratec lists a resonance dampener in Rigid's Bronco roof-rack kit, which is aimed at exactly that. Light covers and a bar set slightly back from the windshield edge can also change the sound. If you spend most of your time on the highway, A-pillar or bumper lights keep the question away from the roof."),
 ("Will 2021–2024 Bronco light brackets fit a 2025 or 2026 Bronco?",
  "Often, but check the year range. Baja lists its A-pillar and fog pocket kits for the 2021–2026 Bronco, while several Amazon titles for the same kits still read 2021–2024, and some budget brackets stop at 2023. Rigid's page says 2021+. The mounting points haven't changed in any source we found, but a listing that names your model year is the safe buy, and the seller is the one to ask when it doesn't."),
]

